IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`
IMPORT `crtpa-s1-application`
IMPORT `crtpa-s2-right`
IMPORT `crtpa-s3-variation`
IMPORT `crtpa-s4-defences`
IMPORT `crtpa-s5-s6-promisee`
IMPORT `crtpa-s7-exceptions`
IMPORT `crtpa-s8-supplementary`
IMPORT `crtpa-s9-arbitration`
IMPORT `crtpa-enforce`

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is not a party to a contract but is named in it or benefits from it, asking on facts they
-- can state whether they may enforce a term, whether the parties may still vary or cancel it, and what defences
-- the promisor has.  This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions
-- that person would ask.  Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for
-- each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  The MAYBE inputs the
-- modules expect are built inside each question, in its body, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then
-- called; no rule is restated here.
--   * A fact the person may not know or may not be able to judge is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure"
--     (`My answer`); "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A sum the person does not know is asked as 0, and becomes NOTHING.
--   * What other Acts say (the Limitation Act 1959, the Bills of Lading Act 1992, the Carriage by Air Act 1988, the
--     Minister's orders) is not among the sources: the person states it, or is not sure.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not
-- answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.  JUST FALSE
-- from a rule about one defence, one exception or one route means that rule gives the person nothing on these
-- facts; it does not mean the contract has no other force (section 8(1)).
--
-- Every question asks about a term, a contract and a promisor the person has in mind.  There is no seat for an
-- official: the court and the arbitral tribunal appear only as the bodies that may dispense with the person's
-- consent and impose conditions (s 3(4) to (7)) and that must reduce an award to the person (s 6), and the person
-- meets those provisions as questions about what may be done to their consent or award.  The regulative rules
-- (s 3(1) SHANT, s 3(4) MAY, s 4(6) SHANT, s 6 MUST) stay in layer 1: on the main build a DEONTIC that leaves an
-- obligation or permission standing cannot be compared in a case, so the person is asked their decision twins, which
-- are the same conditions as yes/no questions.

DECLARE `My answer` IS ONE OF
    Yes
    No
    `I am not sure`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A sum that the person gives as 0 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- Whether the person has a right under section 2, from the facts section 2(1) turns on.
GIVEN `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`my right to enforce the term under section 2 from what I say` MEANS
    `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` `I am a party to the contract` `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` (`what I say, as a fact` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`)

-- Whether section 2 gives the person a right under the carriage exceptions of section 7(5), from the facts they state.
GIVEN `the contract is a contract of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` IS A `My answer`
      `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract` IS A `My answer`
      `the mode of carriage` IS A `Mode of carriage`
      `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` IS A `My answer`
      `I seek only to avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`my carriage exception from what I say` MEANS
    `s 7(5) section 2 confers a right on the third party in the case of the contract`
        (`s 7(5)(a) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` (`s 7(6) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `the contract is a contract of carriage` (`what I say, as a fact` `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill`) (`what I say, as a fact` `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract`)))
        (`s 7(5)(b) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` `the mode of carriage` (`what I say, as a fact` `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention`))
        `I seek only to avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract`

§ `The Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Does the Act reach my contract? (s 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ss 1(2) and (3).  The Act does not apply to a contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from
-- 1 January 2002, unless the contract expressly provides for its application; the text never says in
-- terms that it applies to any contract.  So the answer is JUST FALSE while the restriction bites and NOTHING otherwise (after
-- the 6 months, or where section 1(3) lifts the restriction), and NOTHING there does not mean the Act does not apply.
-- The combined question below (sections 1, 2 and 7 together) treats a restriction that does not bite as no bar.  A date
-- the text does not decide (1 July 2002, where the Interpretation Act cannot count months from a day) also answers
-- NOTHING.
@export Does the Act apply to the contract I am asking about (ss 1(2) and 1(3))?  A NOTHING answer does not mean that the Act does not apply: after the 6 months, or where section 1(3) lifts the restriction, section 1 is silent about whether the Act applies.
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract entered into?
      `the contract expressly provides that the Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 is to apply to it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to my contract` IS
    `s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was entered into` `the contract expressly provides that the Act applies to it`

@export Does the restriction on the Act's application bar me because of when my contract was entered into (s 1(2))?
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract entered into?
      `the contract expressly provides that the Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 is to apply to it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the restriction on the Act's application apply to my contract` IS
    `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` `the date the contract was entered into` `the contract expressly provides that the Act applies to it`

@export Is the restriction on the Act's application lifted for my contract (s 1(3))?
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract entered into?
      `the contract expressly provides that the Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 is to apply to it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the restriction on the Act's application lifted for my contract` IS
    `s 1(3) the restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was entered into` `the contract expressly provides that the Act applies to it`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `May I enforce a term of the contract myself? (s 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Am I a third party to the contract (s 2(1))?
GIVEN `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a third party to the contract` IS
    `s 2(1) the person is a third party` `I am a party to the contract`

-- s 2(1).  A third party may enforce a term if the contract expressly provides that the third party may, or if the term
-- purports to confer a benefit on the third party and, on a proper construction, the parties did not intend it to be
-- enforceable by the third party (s 2(2)) does not take it out.  Whether the parties intended is a judgment of the
-- contract's meaning, which you may answer "I am not sure".
@export May I, in my own right, enforce a term of the contract (s 2(1))?
GIVEN `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the contract?
      `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that you may enforce the term?
      `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to confer a benefit on you?
      `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer` @desc Reading the contract as a whole, does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I enforce a term of the contract in my own right` IS
    (`my right to enforce the term under section 2 from what I say` `I am a party to the contract` `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`)

@export Does the term purport to confer a benefit on me in a way the parties are not taken to have meant to keep from me (ss 2(1)(b) and 2(2))?
GIVEN `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to confer a benefit on you?
      `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer` @desc Reading the contract as a whole, does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the term purport to confer a benefit on me and not fall within the intention exception` IS
    `s 2(1)(b) the term purports to confer a benefit on the third party and subsection (2) does not take it out` `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` (`what I say, as a fact` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`)

@export Does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me, so that s 2(1)(b) does not apply (s 2(2))?
GIVEN `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer` @desc Reading the contract as a whole, does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 2(2) take the term out of section 2(1)(b)` IS
    `s 2(2) subsection (1)(b) does not apply to the term` (`what I say, as a fact` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`)

-- s 2(3).  The third party must be expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as
-- answering a particular description.  Identification by implication only, or no identification, is the text's no on
-- this reading (judgment call QB, NOTES.md).
@export Does the contract identify me in the way section 2(3) requires (s 2(3))?
GIVEN `how the contract identifies me` IS A `Way the third party is identified in the contract` @desc How does the contract identify you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the contract identify me as section 2(3) requires` IS
    `s 2(3) the third party is expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description` `how the contract identifies me`

-- s 2(3).  "The third party need not be in existence when the contract is entered into."  The answer is the text's no
-- whether you were in existence or not.
@export Must I have been in existence when the contract was entered into (s 2(3))?
GIVEN `I was in existence when the contract was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in existence when the contract was entered into?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I have been in existence when the contract was entered into` IS
    `s 2(3) the third party must be in existence when the contract is entered into` `I was in existence when the contract was entered into`

@export Does section 2 give me a right to enforce the term otherwise than subject to the contract's other terms (s 2(4))?
GIVEN `my enforcing the term would be subject to and in accordance with the other relevant terms of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your enforcing the term be subject to, and in accordance with, the other relevant terms of the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 2 give me a right to enforce otherwise than subject to the contract's other terms` IS
    `s 2(4) section 2 confers a right on the third party to enforce the term otherwise than subject to and in accordance with the other relevant terms of the contract` `my enforcing the term would be subject to and in accordance with the other relevant terms of the contract`

-- s 2(5).  Subject to the Act, there is available to the third party who has a right to enforce a term every remedy
-- that would have been available to the third party in an action for breach of contract if the third party had been a
-- party to the contract.
@export Is the remedy I want available to me (s 2(5))?
GIVEN `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the contract?
      `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that you may enforce the term?
      `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to confer a benefit on you?
      `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer` @desc Reading the contract as a whole, does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by you?
      `the remedy would have been available to me in an action for breach of contract if I had been a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the remedy you want have been available to you in an action for breach of contract if you had been a party to the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the remedy I want available to me` IS
    `s 2(5) the remedy is available to the third party` (`my right to enforce the term under section 2 from what I say` `I am a party to the contract` `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`) `the remedy would have been available to me in an action for breach of contract if I had been a party to the contract`

@export Do the rules on damages, injunctions, specific performance and other remedies apply to my remedy (s 2(5))?
GIVEN `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the contract?
      `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that you may enforce the term?
      `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to confer a benefit on you?
      `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer` @desc Reading the contract as a whole, does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the rules on damages, injunctions and other remedies apply to my remedy` IS
    `s 2(5) the rules relating to damages, injunctions, specific performance and other remedy apply to the third party's remedy accordingly` (`my right to enforce the term under section 2 from what I say` `I am a party to the contract` `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`)

@export May the promisor refuse me a remedy on the ground that I am a volunteer (s 2(5))?
GIVEN `the ground for refusing the remedy is that, as against the promisor, I am a volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground on which the promisor would refuse the remedy that, as against the promisor, you are a volunteer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the promisor refuse me a remedy because I am a volunteer` IS
    `s 2(5) the remedy may be refused on the ground that, as against the promisor, the third party is a volunteer` `the ground for refusing the remedy is that, as against the promisor, I am a volunteer`

@export Is a reference to my enforcing the term to be read as my availing myself of an exclusion or limitation (s 2(6))?
GIVEN `the kind of term` IS A `Kind of term` @desc Is the term one that excludes or limits liability in relation to a matter, or is it any other term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a reference to my enforcing the term to be read as my availing myself of an exclusion or limitation` IS
    `s 2(6) references in this Act to the third party enforcing the term are to be construed as references to availing of the exclusion or limitation` `the kind of term`

@export What is a reference to my enforcing the term to be read as (s 2(6))?
GIVEN `the kind of term` IS A `Kind of term` @desc Is the term one that excludes or limits liability in relation to a matter, or is it any other term?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Meaning of a reference to enforcing a term`
DECIDE `What a reference to my enforcing the term is to be read as` IS
    `s 2(6) what a reference to the third party enforcing the term is construed as` `the kind of term`

@export Is the party I am asking about the promisee (s 2(7))?
GIVEN `the term is enforceable by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the term one that a third party can enforce under section 2?
      `where the party stands` IS A `Position of a party in relation to the term` @desc Where does the party you are asking about stand in relation to the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the party I am asking about the promisee` IS
    `s 2(7) the party is the promisee` `the term is enforceable by a third party` `where the party stands`

@export Is the party I am asking about the promisor (s 2(7))?
GIVEN `the term is enforceable by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the term one that a third party can enforce under section 2?
      `where the party stands` IS A `Position of a party in relation to the term` @desc Where does the party you are asking about stand in relation to the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the party I am asking about the promisor` IS
    `s 2(7) the party is the promisor` `the term is enforceable by a third party` `where the party stands`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `May the parties cancel or change my right? (s 3)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 3(1).  (a) I have communicated my assent to the term to the promisor; or (b) the promisor is aware that I have
-- relied on the term; or (c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that I would rely on the term and
-- I have in fact relied on it.
@export Has one of the circumstances in section 3(1)(a), (b) and (c) arisen (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `I have communicated my assent to the term to the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you communicated your assent to the term to the promisor?
      `the promisor is aware that I have relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the promisor aware that you have relied on the term?
      `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that I would rely on the term` IS A `My answer` @desc Can the promisor reasonably be expected to have foreseen that you would rely on the term?
      `I have in fact relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you in fact relied on the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has one of the circumstances in section 3(1) arisen` IS
    `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` `I have communicated my assent to the term to the promisor` `the promisor is aware that I have relied on the term` (`what I say, as a fact` `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that I would rely on the term`) `I have in fact relied on the term`

@export Is it a condition of s 3(1)(b) and (c) that I know the precise terms of the term (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `I have knowledge of the precise terms of the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the precise terms of the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is knowledge of the precise terms a condition of section 3(1)(b) and (c)` IS
    `s 3(1)(b) and (c) knowledge of the precise terms of the term is a condition` `I have knowledge of the precise terms of the term`

@export May I give my assent in this form (s 3(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the form of my assent` IS A `Form of the third party's assent` @desc In what form did you give your assent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I give my assent in this form` IS
    `s 3(2)(a) the assent may be by this form` `the form of my assent`

-- s 3(2)(b).  An assent sent by post or other means is not regarded as communicated to the promisor until it is received
-- by the promisor.  Before receipt the answer is the text's yes; once received the text stops speaking of it.
@export Can my assent not yet be regarded as communicated to the promisor (s 3(2)(b))?
GIVEN `my assent was sent to the promisor by post or other means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send your assent to the promisor by post or other means?
      `the promisor has received my assent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the promisor received your assent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my assent not yet be regarded as communicated to the promisor` IS
    `s 3(2)(b) the assent cannot yet be regarded as communicated to the promisor` `my assent was sent to the promisor by post or other means` `the promisor has received my assent`

@export Has my assent been communicated to the promisor (s 3(2)(b))?
GIVEN `my assent was sent to the promisor by post or other means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send your assent to the promisor by post or other means?
      `the promisor has received my assent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the promisor received your assent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my assent been communicated to the promisor` IS
    `s 3(2)(b) the assent has been communicated to the promisor` `my assent was sent to the promisor by post or other means` `the promisor has received my assent`

-- s 3(1).  Where I have a right under section 2 to enforce a term, the parties to the contract may not, by agreement,
-- rescind the contract or vary it in such a way as to extinguish or alter my entitlement under that right, without my
-- consent, if one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) has arisen.  Section 3(1) is silent on a change of the
-- contract otherwise than by the parties' agreement.
@export Are the parties to the contract barred from rescinding or varying the contract without my consent (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the contract?
      `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that you may enforce the term?
      `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to confer a benefit on you?
      `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer` @desc Reading the contract as a whole, does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by you?
      `what the parties do` IS A `What the parties do by agreement` @desc What are the parties to the contract doing to it?
      `I have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to what the parties are doing?
      `I have communicated my assent to the term to the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you communicated your assent to the term to the promisor?
      `the promisor is aware that I have relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the promisor aware that you have relied on the term?
      `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that I would rely on the term` IS A `My answer` @desc Can the promisor reasonably be expected to have foreseen that you would rely on the term?
      `I have in fact relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you in fact relied on the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the parties barred from rescinding or varying the contract without my consent` IS
    `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (`my right to enforce the term under section 2 from what I say` `I am a party to the contract` `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`) `what the parties do` `I have consented` (`s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` `I have communicated my assent to the term to the promisor` `the promisor is aware that I have relied on the term` (`what I say, as a fact` `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that I would rely on the term`) `I have in fact relied on the term`)

@export Are the parties barred from rescinding or varying the contract without my consent, taking the contract's own terms about consent into account (ss 3(1) and 3(3))?
GIVEN `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the contract?
      `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that you may enforce the term?
      `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to confer a benefit on you?
      `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer` @desc Reading the contract as a whole, does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by you?
      `what the parties do` IS A `What the parties do by agreement` @desc What are the parties to the contract doing to it?
      `I have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to what the parties are doing?
      `I have communicated my assent to the term to the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you communicated your assent to the term to the promisor?
      `the promisor is aware that I have relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the promisor aware that you have relied on the term?
      `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that I would rely on the term` IS A `My answer` @desc Can the promisor reasonably be expected to have foreseen that you would rely on the term?
      `I have in fact relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you in fact relied on the term?
      `the express term of the contract about consent` IS A `Express term of the contract about consent` @desc Does the contract have an express term about when your consent is needed?
      `the circumstances the contract specifies exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the contract specifies circumstances in which your consent is required, do those circumstances exist?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the parties barred from rescinding or varying the contract without my consent given the contract's own terms` IS
    `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (`my right to enforce the term under section 2 from what I say` `I am a party to the contract` `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`) `what the parties do` `I have consented` (`s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` `I have communicated my assent to the term to the promisor` `the promisor is aware that I have relied on the term` (`what I say, as a fact` `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that I would rely on the term`) `I have in fact relied on the term`) `the express term of the contract about consent` `the circumstances the contract specifies exist`

@export May the court or arbitral tribunal dispense with my consent (s 3(4))?
GIVEN `my consent is required under section 3(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your consent required to the rescission or variation under section 3(1) or (3)?
      `the parties to the contract have applied to the court or arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to the contract applied to the court or arbitral tribunal?
      `the court or tribunal is satisfied that my consent cannot be obtained because my whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the court or tribunal satisfied that your consent cannot be obtained because your whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained?
      `the court or tribunal is satisfied that I am mentally incapable of giving my consent` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the court or tribunal satisfied that you are mentally incapable of giving your consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court or arbitral tribunal dispense with my consent` IS
    `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` `my consent is required under section 3(1) or (3)` `the parties to the contract have applied to the court or arbitral tribunal` (`what I say, as a fact` `the court or tribunal is satisfied that my consent cannot be obtained because my whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained`) (`what I say, as a fact` `the court or tribunal is satisfied that I am mentally incapable of giving my consent`)

@export May the court or arbitral tribunal dispense with a consent of mine that may be required under section 3(1)(c) (s 3(5))?
GIVEN `the consent is one that may be required under section 3(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consent one that may be required under section 3(1)(c), that is, because the promisor could be expected to foresee your reliance and you in fact relied?
      `the parties to the contract have applied to the court or arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties to the contract applied to the court or arbitral tribunal?
      `the court or tribunal is satisfied that it cannot reasonably be ascertained whether or not I have in fact relied on the term` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the court or tribunal satisfied that it cannot reasonably be ascertained whether or not you have in fact relied on the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court or arbitral tribunal dispense with a consent of mine under section 3(1)(c)` IS
    `s 3(5) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with a consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` `the consent is one that may be required under section 3(1)(c)` `the parties to the contract have applied to the court or arbitral tribunal` (`what I say, as a fact` `the court or tribunal is satisfied that it cannot reasonably be ascertained whether or not I have in fact relied on the term`)

@export May the court or arbitral tribunal impose such conditions as it thinks fit when it dispenses with my consent (s 3(6))?
GIVEN `the court or arbitral tribunal has dispensed with my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court or arbitral tribunal dispensed with your consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court or arbitral tribunal impose conditions when it dispenses with my consent` IS
    `s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose such conditions as it thinks fit` `the court or arbitral tribunal has dispensed with my consent`

@export May the court or arbitral tribunal require compensation to be paid to me as a condition of dispensing with my consent (s 3(6))?
GIVEN `the court or arbitral tribunal has dispensed with my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court or arbitral tribunal dispensed with your consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court or arbitral tribunal require compensation to be paid to me` IS
    `s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose a condition requiring the payment of compensation to the third party` `the court or arbitral tribunal has dispensed with my consent`

@export May this body exercise the jurisdiction to dispense with my consent (s 3(7))?
GIVEN `the body` IS A `Forum` @desc Which body is being asked to exercise the jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this body exercise the jurisdiction to dispense with my consent` IS
    `s 3(7) the jurisdiction conferred on the court by subsections (4), (5) and (6) is exercisable by this body` `the body`

