      `an express term of the contract provides for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings I bring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an express term of the contract provide for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings you bring?
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the promisee had brought the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the matter have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the promisee had brought the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
