-- s 4(4)(b).  JUST FALSE here is "this subsection gives the promisor no defence on these facts", not "the promisor has no defence at all":
-- the matter may fall inside another subsection of section 4 or inside the general law the Act leaves alone.
@export Is the matter available to the promisor by way of counterclaim as it would have been against me had I been a party to the contract (s 4(4)(b))?
