-- A convenience gathered by hand in layer 1 (ruling E1, option B as guidance only): the three routes to the same
-- effect, each of which has its own question above.  JUST FALSE is "none of these three gives the promisor the matter
-- on these facts", not "the promisor has no defence at all".
@export Is the matter available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off under section 4(2), (3) or (4)(a), taken together?
GIVEN `I am bringing proceedings to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you bringing proceedings to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2?
      `the matter arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter the promisor raises arise from or in connection with the contract, and is it relevant to the term?
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the promisee had brought the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the matter have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the promisee had brought the proceedings?
      `an express term of the contract provides for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings I bring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an express term of the contract provide for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings you bring?
      `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off against me if I had been a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the matter have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off against you if you had been a party to the contract?
      `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an express term of the contract provide that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the matter available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off, taking section 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) together` IS
    `s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` `I am bringing proceedings to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2` `the matter arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term` `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off if the promisee had brought the proceedings` `an express term of the contract provides for the matter to be available to the promisor in proceedings I bring` `the matter would have been available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off against me if I had been a party to the contract` `an express term of the contract provides that the matter is not to be available to the promisor by way of defence, set-off or counterclaim`

@export Am I barred from enforcing the term in the proceedings brought against me (s 4(6))?
GIVEN `proceedings are brought against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are proceedings brought against you?
      `I seek to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you seek to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2?
      `I could not have done so had I been a party to the contract` IS A `My answer` @desc Could you not have done so had you been a party to the contract, whether because of particular circumstances relating to you or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from enforcing the term in the proceedings brought against me` IS
    `s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` `proceedings are brought against me` `I seek to enforce a term of the contract in reliance on section 2` (`what I say, as a fact` `I could not have done so had I been a party to the contract`)

