    `s 7(4) section 2 confers a right on the third party to enforce a term of the contract of employment against an employee` `the contract is a contract of employment` `I seek to enforce the term against an employee`

-- s 7(5).  Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of a contract for the carriage of goods by sea,
-- or a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road or of cargo by air which is subject to the rules of the
-- appropriate international transport convention, except that a third party may in reliance on that section avail
-- itself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in such a contract.  A lifted bar grants nothing here (judgment
-- call QA); the grant is the next question.
@export Does section 2 give me a right in the case of a contract of carriage (s 7(5))?
GIVEN `the contract is a contract of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a contract of carriage?
      `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the carriage contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill?
      `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract` IS A `My answer` @desc Is an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order given under or for the purposes of the contract?
      `the mode of carriage` IS A `Mode of carriage` @desc What is carried under the contract, and by what mode? Choose the cargo-by-air, goods-by-rail or goods-by-road answer only when the contract is for carrying goods (by air, cargo) in that way; for passengers or baggage, or anything else that is not goods or cargo, choose the answer that says something other than cargo or goods. Section 7(5)(b) and 7(6) name only goods by rail, goods by road and cargo by air.
      `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the contract subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention?
      `I seek only to avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you seek only to avail yourself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 2 give me a right under a contract of carriage` IS
    (`my carriage exception from what I say` `the contract is a contract of carriage` `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract` `the mode of carriage` `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` `I seek only to avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract`)

@export May I, in reliance on section 2, avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in a contract of carriage (s 7(5))?
GIVEN `the contract is a contract of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a contract of carriage?
      `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the carriage contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill?
      `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract` IS A `My answer` @desc Is an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order given under or for the purposes of the contract?
      `the mode of carriage` IS A `Mode of carriage` @desc What is carried under the contract, and by what mode? Choose the cargo-by-air, goods-by-rail or goods-by-road answer only when the contract is for carrying goods (by air, cargo) in that way; for passengers or baggage, or anything else that is not goods or cargo, choose the answer that says something other than cargo or goods. Section 7(5)(b) and 7(6) name only goods by rail, goods by road and cargo by air.
      `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the contract subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention?
      `I seek only to avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you seek only to avail yourself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in a contract of carriage` IS
    `s 7(5) the third party may in reliance on section 2 avail of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract` (`s 7(5)(a) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` (`s 7(6) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `the contract is a contract of carriage` (`what I say, as a fact` `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill`) (`what I say, as a fact` `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract`))) (`s 7(5)(b) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` `the mode of carriage` (`what I say, as a fact` `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention`)) `I seek only to avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract`

@export Is my contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea (s 7(6))?
GIVEN `the contract is a contract of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a contract of carriage?
      `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the carriage contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill?
      `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract` IS A `My answer` @desc Is an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order given under or for the purposes of the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contract a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS
    `s 7(6) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `the contract is a contract of carriage` (`what I say, as a fact` `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill`) (`what I say, as a fact` `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract`)

@export Is this Convention the appropriate international transport convention for my contract (s 7(6))?
GIVEN `the mode of carriage` IS A `Mode of carriage` @desc What is carried under the contract, and by what mode? Choose the cargo-by-air, goods-by-rail or goods-by-road answer only when the contract is for carrying goods (by air, cargo) in that way; for passengers or baggage, or anything else that is not goods or cargo, choose the answer that says something other than cargo or goods. Section 7(5)(b) and 7(6) name only goods by rail, goods by road and cargo by air.
      `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under section 3 of the Carriage by Air Act 1988` IS A `My answer` @desc Does the Convention have the force of law in Singapore under section 3 of the Carriage by Air Act 1988?
      `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under a written law the Minister has by order prescribed` IS A `My answer` @desc Does the Convention have the force of law in Singapore under a written law that the Minister has prescribed by order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this Convention the appropriate international transport convention for my contract` IS
    `s 7(6) the Convention is the appropriate international transport convention for the contract` `the mode of carriage` (`what I say, as a fact` `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under section 3 of the Carriage by Air Act 1988`) (`what I say, as a fact` `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under a written law the Minister has by order prescribed`)

@export Does this document have the meaning the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives to its name (s 7(7))?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Shipping document` @desc Which document are you asking about?
      `the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives the document that name` IS A `My answer` @desc Does the Bills of Lading Act 1992 give the document that name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this document have the meaning the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives to its name` IS
    `s 7(7) the document has the meaning given by the Bills of Lading Act 1992 for its name` `the document` (`what I say, as a fact` `the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives the document that name`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What else does the Act leave in place, or change? (s 8)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Does section 2 affect a right or remedy of mine that exists or is available apart from the Act (s 8(1))?
GIVEN `the right or remedy exists or is available to me apart from this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the right or remedy exist, or is it available to you, apart from this Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 2 affect a right or remedy of mine that exists apart from the Act` IS
    `s 8(1) section 2 affects a right or remedy of the third party that exists or is available apart from this Act` `the right or remedy exists or is available to me apart from this Act`

@export Does section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 not apply to my claim (s 8(2))?
GIVEN `the negligence consists of the breach of an obligation arising from a term of a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the negligence consist of the breach of an obligation arising from a term of a contract?
      `the person seeking to enforce the obligation is a third party acting in reliance on section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person seeking to enforce the obligation a third party acting in reliance on section 2?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 not apply to my claim` IS
    `s 8(2) section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 does not apply` `the negligence consists of the breach of an obligation arising from a term of a contract` `the person seeking to enforce the obligation is a third party acting in reliance on section 2`

@export Is my action one founded on a contract for the purposes of section 6 of the Limitation Act 1959 (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `the action is brought in reliance on section 2 relating to a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your action brought in reliance on section 2 relating to a contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my action one founded on a contract for the purposes of the Limitation Act 1959` IS
    `s 8(3) the action is one founded on a contract for the purposes of section 6 of the Limitation Act 1959` `the action is brought in reliance on section 2 relating to a contract`

-- s 8(3) adds my action to the actions section 6 of the Limitation Act 1959 reaches; the period itself is that Act's,
-- which is not among the sources, so you give it or the answer is NOTHING.
@export What period, in years, applies to my action (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `the action is brought in reliance on section 2 relating to a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your action brought in reliance on section 2 relating to a contract?
      `the period section 6 of the Limitation Act 1959 gives for an action founded on a contract, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What period, in years, does section 6 of the Limitation Act 1959 give for an action founded on a contract? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What period in years applies to my action` IS
    `s 8(3) the period that applies to the action, in years` `the action is brought in reliance on section 2 relating to a contract` (`my amount if I know it` `the period section 6 of the Limitation Act 1959 gives for an action founded on a contract, in years`)

@export Am I treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of any other written law (s 8(4))?
GIVEN `the route` IS A `Route by which the third party might be treated as a party` @desc By what route might you be treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of another written law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of another written law` IS
    `s 8(4) the third party is treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of any other written law` `the route`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What if the contract has an arbitration term? (s 9)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Am I treated as a party to the arbitration agreement for disputes about my enforcing the term (s 9(1))?
GIVEN `I have a right under section 2 to enforce the substantive term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right under section 2 to enforce the term (the substantive term)?
      `my right is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your right subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration?
      `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` IS A `Arbitration statute` @desc Is the arbitration agreement an agreement in writing for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001, of Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994, or of neither?
      `the dispute asked about` IS A `Dispute asked about` @desc Which dispute are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as a party to the arbitration agreement for disputes about my enforcing the term` IS
    `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` `I have a right under section 2 to enforce the substantive term` `my right is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration` `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` `the dispute asked about`

@export For the purposes of which Act am I treated as a party to the arbitration agreement (s 9(1))?
GIVEN `I have a right under section 2 to enforce the substantive term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right under section 2 to enforce the term (the substantive term)?
      `my right is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your right subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration?
      `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` IS A `Arbitration statute` @desc Is the arbitration agreement an agreement in writing for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001, of Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994, or of neither?
      `the dispute asked about` IS A `Dispute asked about` @desc Which dispute are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Arbitration statute`
DECIDE `For the purposes of which Act am I treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` IS
    `s 9(1) the Act for the purposes of which the third party is treated as a party` `I have a right under section 2 to enforce the substantive term` `my right is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to arbitration` `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` `the dispute asked about`

@export Am I treated as a party to the arbitration agreement because I exercise the right (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `I have a right under section 2 to enforce a term providing for one or more descriptions of dispute between me and the promisor to be submitted to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right under section 2 to enforce a term providing for one or more descriptions of dispute between you and the promisor to be submitted to arbitration?
      `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` IS A `Arbitration statute` @desc Is the arbitration agreement an agreement in writing for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001, of Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994, or of neither?
      `I fall to be treated under section 9(1) as a party to the arbitration agreement` IS A `My answer` @desc Do you fall to be treated under section 9(1) as a party to the arbitration agreement?
      `I exercise the right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you exercise the right?
      `the time asked about` IS A `Time asked about, relative to the exercise of the right` @desc At what time, relative to your exercise of the right, are you asking whether you are treated as a party to the arbitration agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as a party to the arbitration agreement because I exercise the right` IS
    `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` `I have a right under section 2 to enforce a term providing for one or more descriptions of dispute between me and the promisor to be submitted to arbitration` `the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of` (`what I say, as a fact` `I fall to be treated under section 9(1) as a party to the arbitration agreement`) `I exercise the right` `the time asked about`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Taking it all together: may I enforce the term? (ss 1, 2 and 7)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A convenience gathered by hand in layer 1 (ruling E1, option B as guidance only): it combines the answers of the
-- questions above and holds no law of its own.  JUST FALSE is "the Act gives no right to enforce on these facts"; it
-- is not a finding that the contract has no other force (s 8(1)).  NOTHING means the Act does not decide it on these
-- facts.
@export Taking sections 1, 2 and 7 together, may I enforce a term of the contract (ss 1, 2 and 7)?
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract entered into?
      `the contract expressly provides that the Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 is to apply to it?
      `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the contract?
      `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract expressly provide that you may enforce the term?
      `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to confer a benefit on you?
      `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me` IS A `My answer` @desc Reading the contract as a whole, does it appear that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by you?
      `how the contract identifies me` IS A `Way the third party is identified in the contract` @desc How does the contract identify you?
      `my enforcing the term would be subject to and in accordance with the other relevant terms of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your enforcing the term be subject to, and in accordance with, the other relevant terms of the contract?
      `the contract is a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument?
      `the contract is a contract binding on a company and its members under section 39 of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract one that binds a company and its members under section 39 of the Companies Act 1967?
      `the contract is a registration document of a limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a registration document of a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005?
      `the contract is a limited liability partnership agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a limited liability partnership agreement as defined in that Act?
      `the contract is a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a contract of employment?
      `I seek to enforce the term against an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you seek to enforce the term against an employee?
      `the contract is a contract of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a contract of carriage?
      `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the carriage contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill?
      `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract` IS A `My answer` @desc Is an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order given under or for the purposes of the contract?
      `the mode of carriage` IS A `Mode of carriage` @desc What is carried under the contract, and by what mode? Choose the cargo-by-air, goods-by-rail or goods-by-road answer only when the contract is for carrying goods (by air, cargo) in that way; for passengers or baggage, or anything else that is not goods or cargo, choose the answer that says something other than cargo or goods. Section 7(5)(b) and 7(6) name only goods by rail, goods by road and cargo by air.
      `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the contract subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention?
      `I seek only to avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you seek only to avail yourself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Taking sections 1, 2 and 7 together may I enforce a term` IS
    `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (`s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` `the date the contract was entered into` `the contract expressly provides that the Act applies to it`) (`my right to enforce the term under section 2 from what I say` `I am a party to the contract` `the contract expressly provides that I may enforce the term` `the term purports to confer a benefit on me` `on a proper construction of the contract it appears that the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable by me`) (`s 2(3) the third party is expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description` `how the contract identifies me`) (`s 2(4) section 2 confers a right on the third party to enforce the term otherwise than subject to and in accordance with the other relevant terms of the contract` `my enforcing the term would be subject to and in accordance with the other relevant terms of the contract`) (LIST (`s 7(1) section 2 confers a right on the third party in the case of the contract` `the contract is a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument`), (`s 7(2) section 2 confers a right on the third party in the case of the contract` `the contract is a contract binding on a company and its members under section 39 of the Companies Act 1967`), (`s 7(3) section 2 confers a right on the third party in the case of the contract` `the contract is a registration document of a limited liability partnership` `the contract is a limited liability partnership agreement`), (`s 7(4) section 2 confers a right on the third party to enforce a term of the contract of employment against an employee` `the contract is a contract of employment` `I seek to enforce the term against an employee`), (`my carriage exception from what I say` `the contract is a contract of carriage` `the carriage is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of the contract` `the mode of carriage` `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` `I seek only to avail myself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract`))
